rol by regulating levels of lysine-specific demethylase 4A. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2013].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9UKA2","text":"Substrate-recognition component of the mitochondria-localized SCF-FBXL4 ubiquitin E3 ligase complex that plays a role in the restriction of mitophagy by controlling the degradation of BNIP3 and NIX mitophagy receptors (PubMed:36896912, PubMed:38992176). Rescues also mitochondrial injury through reverting hyperactivation of DRP1-mediated mitochondrial fission (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}